it ends up being just as bad as a payday loan. And $2.99 doesn't seem that bad or $3.99 doesn't seem that bad. $3.99 every single day. Now, again, you're just eating away at your hard-earned money. What about the movement toward a cashless society? I mean, a lot of us never have any money in our pockets anymore because we don't need to. we live off of credit cards. How is that affecting how people spend and save today?

