00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:38.000
Well, the first thing I want to say is that, you know, we're just exacerbating inequality. There is a large swath of the population that's unbanked or underbanked, meaning that there's a large part of the population that is being forced into a cashless society. In order to get a bank account in the U.S., you need an address. Like fundamentally, right? And we don't think about that.

34
00:26:38.000 --> 00:27:13.000
But with houselessness being on the rise, in order to get a bank account in the U.S., you need a social security number or a tax ID number. We have millions of people who are relying on the cash economy. And so when you have restaurants that say, no, we only accept debit cards. When you have restaurants or businesses that say, no, we only accept, you know, Apple Pay, it's a form of exacerbating inequality and creating this two-tier system between the halves and the half-nots.

