00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:52.000
Now, putting that, you know, having said that, what then happens to people when you're constantly having to not to not just take out your credit card anymore? Right, now it's a tap. Well, we distance ourselves from what researchers call the pain of pain, meaning it doesn't feel like you're really wasting any money if you just tap your phone. If when you're at Starbucks, right? And when we disassociate ourselves from the pain of pain because we don't viscerally see the money leaving, because it doesn't feel like we're spending anything, then it increases our likelihood of spending.

